  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds will provide support for essential security operations and rhino monitoring for eastern black rhinos in Chyulu Hills National Park in Kenya. Specific activities will include constructing a new ranger base in an area that was previously difficult to secure, providing basic and advanced ranger training for the community scouts, deploying community scouts for general security and specialized scouts for rhino monitoring, maintaining a network of satellite camera traps and the rhino identification database, and deploying tracking equipment on one or more rhinos to better understand their behavior and habitat use.</narrative>
  </description>
